Add a token-bucket rate limiter to this directory as ratelimiter.py -- the only new file to create.

class TokenBucket:
    def __init__(self, capacity: int, refill_rate: float, clock: Callable[[], float] | None = None)
    def allow(self) -> bool

The bucket starts full (capacity tokens available). Each call to allow() first adds tokens for the time elapsed since the last call (or since construction, on the first call) at refill_rate tokens per second, capped at capacity, then consumes and returns True if at least one token is now available, or returns False and consumes nothing otherwise. clock is a zero-argument callable returning the current time in seconds; default to time.monotonic when omitted.

test_ratelimiter.py already exists in this directory and is the fixed check for this task -- do not change it. Do not create or modify any file other than ratelimiter.py.
